-- marks.rite — the class-marks, spoken by a rite that wears them correctly.
--
-- Determinatives were recorded and read by nothing from 2026-07-11 until 2026-07-24.
-- They now do three small, decidable things (SPEC §IV.b) and one beautiful one (§IV.d).
-- Read this rite before performing it:  ordo attend ordo/rites/marks.rite

In the worship register, canon living.

-- The marks are semantic class and nothing else. Canon says so in the same chapter
-- that invented them, and lists evidentiality among what they do not cover.
Let claim be the definition of diplosemy.ABS.
Speak claim.

-- A word carries the mark canon assigns it. Written agreement is silent; a written
-- disagreement is said, with the line of canon that settles it.
Speak verisleight.HID.
Speak dokimance.ACT.

-- What ORDO refuses to do here is as much the point. The .HID class holds lanthes
-- (to escape notice — agentless, blameless) beside verisleight (truth arranged to
-- deceive). A guard that read the tag as suspicion would have flagged the cathedral's
-- own sigame, where withholding is a received-ordinance and a gift.
Let withheld be the gap of sigame.
Speak withheld.

-- The arithmetic of the honest kind: counted from a report, so born -chu, and no
-- attestation above it will stand.
Let breadth be count of claim.
I attest that breadth is greater than 10 -chu.

Dokimance: breadth is greater than 10.

-- The apophatic edge. doxakallos carries .DIV by canon, so the silence that follows
-- this address is not merely the end of a rite: it is limit-silence, the third silence,
-- which ORDO recognizes rather than keywords (grammars/worship/silence.md:96).
-- What lies beyond the said is honoured here, not asserted.
O-doxakallos.DIV, I acknowledge "the beauty that is glory".
Hesychia.
